      ],
      "message": "validation: don't treat snapshot block as linked on startup\n\nIf the snapshot block is received during background sync before some\nof its ancestors, ReceivedBlockTransactions() adds it to\nm_blocks_unlinked and it isn't a background candidate until the\nmissing blocks arrive.\n\nLoadBlockIndex() doesn't restore this on restart. The snapshot block\ngets its m_chain_tx_count from the assumeutxo data and is never added\nto m_blocks_unlinked, so PopulateBlockIndexCandidates() makes it a\nbackground candidate. FindMostWorkChain() then walks back to its\nparent, which has m_chain_tx_count 0, and hits the HaveNumChainTxs()\nassert. This happens on every restart.\n\nAdd the block to m_blocks_unlinked on startup if an ancestor is\nmissing, and skip it as a background candidate until then. Without\nthe m_blocks_unlinked entry the block isn't picked up when the\nmissing blocks arrive, and background validation stalls.\n\nExtend feature_assumeutxo.py to restart the node in this state.",
